

(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[1 1 "//go:build linux"] [19 1 "// posix's process and file functions (PY6e; Modules/posixmodule.c): stat_result with its float and nanosecond"] [20 1 "// times, scandir and DirEntry, the descriptors' functions (dup2, pread, readv, inheritable and blocking flags),"] [21 1 "// the processes' (waitpid, wait3, wait4, execv, execve, system, times, uname), sysconf, confstr and pathconf over"] [22 1 "// musl's tables, statvfs, the terminal's few (isatty from the device's major number). posix has no fork: Go's"] [23 1 "// runtime is multithreaded, so pyi starts children only through _posixsubprocess.fork_exec (Go's ForkExec), and"] [24 1 "// test.support's has_fork_support is False (the class no-fork)."] [46 2 "// stat_result(seq) of ten: its float times from the int slots (statresult_new)"] [75 1 "// fildesFns are the functions whose descriptor is fildes_converter's (a negative one a ValueError); the others take"] [76 1 "// `int fd` (queue 249)."] [79 1 "// fdArg is a file descriptor argument: an int, or an object's fileno()."] [121 1 "// isattyFd is isatty(3) without its ioctl: a character device of a terminal's major number (tty, console, pts)."] [122 1 "// isattyFd is musl's isatty: TIOCGWINSZ succeeds (queue 220: the ioctl's struct by its address, termios'; before, the"] [123 1 "// device's major number, which missed a pty's master)."] [130 1 "// stdFdValid is pylifecycle.c's is_valid_fd: fstat succeeds on the descriptor (queue 551, the standard streams)."] [136 1 "// pathOrFd is a path argument that may also be a descriptor (os.stat(fd)): path_converter with allow_fd, a bool a"] [137 1 "// descriptor after a RuntimeWarning as _fd_converter warns."] [159 1 "// posixWarnHook is warnings.warn(msg, category), set by makePosix for the converters' warnings."] [162 1 "// fdConv is _fd_converter: an int (a bool warns first) within C's int."] [183 1 "// isBytesPath is a path argument that is bytes, or os.PathLike of bytes: the results are bytes then."] [199 1 "// nameDecode is os.fsdecode of a name: UTF-8, an undecodable byte a surrogate (surrogateescape)."] [218 1 "// fildesWarns are the functions whose descriptor is CPython's fildes converter, which warns of a bool."] [221 1 "// fdDir marks listdir's and scandir's directory given as a descriptor."] [224 1 "// atFdCwd is AT_FDCWD, dir_fd's default."] [227 1 "// dirFd is a dir_fd argument by its keyword (dir_fd_converter): absent or None the current directory, else a"] [228 1 "// descriptor."] [240 1 "// atPath is the *at functions' path: p relative to the directory dirfd as a path the plain calls take, an"] [241 1 "// absolute path or one of the current directory unchanged, else /proc/self/fd/DIRFD/p, the descriptor checked"] [242 1 "// first so that a bad one is EBADF and a file's ENOTDIR, as openat(2) answers (Go's syscall has no linkat,"] [243 1 "// readlinkat, symlinkat or flags for unlinkat; every *at goes this one way)."] [261 1 "// noFollowPath is a path naming the symbolic link p itself, for the calls that have no l* form in Go's syscall"] [262 1 "// (utimensat's AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW): /proc/self/fd/N of an O_PATH|O_NOFOLLOW descriptor, closed by done."] [271 24 "// O_PATH, the same on amd64 and arm64"] [273 1 "// atArgs are a path function's dir_fd and follow_symlinks checked as CPython checks them: fd with dir_fd or"] [274 1 "// follow_symlinks=False is a ValueError."] [303 1 "// splitKw is a call's positional arguments and its keyword ones by name."] [343 2 "// CPython's on musl Linux but those of functions pyi lacks (ptsname_r):"] [344 2 "// the *at functions through atPath, futimens and lutimes through /proc/self/fd"] [375 5 "// CPython's `int fd` (not _PyLong_FileDescriptor_Converter): a negative descriptor reaches the system"] [376 5 "// call, OSError EBADF (queue 249: asyncio's _sock_sendfile_native reads os.fstat(-1)'s OSError as"] [377 5 "// \"not a regular file\")"] [403 2 "// ---- stat"] [420 37 "// lstat takes no descriptor"] [492 19 "// AT_EACCESS"] [495 19 "// AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW"] [585 4 "// fchmodat(AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW) as musl answers it: a link's mode cannot change (EOPNOTSUPP, which"] [586 4 "// os_chmod_impl turns into NotImplementedError), anything else's does"] [722 5 "// linkat(AT_SYMLINK_FOLLOW) by default: the link's target linked, not the link"] [792 44 "// futimens(fd)"] [878 27 "// NODEV"] [895 28 "// makedev(NODEV, NODEV)"] [955 2 "// ---- listdir, scandir"] [969 4 "// fdopendir(dup(fd)) as a fresh open of the descriptor's directory, its entries' paths their names"] [1052 2 "// ---- descriptors"] [1193 2 "// queue 537: the pseudo-terminal functions (posixmodule.c's over musl 1.2.6's: posix_openpt opens /dev/ptmx with"] [1194 2 "// the flags and O_CLOEXEC, grantpt does nothing, unlockpt is TIOCSPTLCK 0, ptsname TIOCGPTN's /dev/pts/N)"] [1195 2 "// METH_O: one positional argument, \"posix.NAME() takes exactly one argument (N given)\""] [1205 2 "// fildes is _PyLong_FileDescriptor_Converter (PyObject_AsFileDescriptor): an int or an object's fileno(); a float"] [1206 2 "// has neither"] [1273 3 "// no TIOCGWINSZ without unsafe: the size the environment gives, else 80x24"] [1393 3 "// the GIL released while it blocks, as posixmodule.c's Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS (PY7: a blocking socket's sendfile"] [1394 3 "// held it, so the thread reading the other end never ran: test_socket's SendfileUsingSendfileTest.testOffset)"] [1416 2 "// ---- processes"] [1507 37 "// -X cpu_count, PYTHON_CPU_COUNT (py-eval-1122)"] [1526 37 "// the kernel's 40..1, as libc's -20..19"] [1575 73 "// the GIL released while it blocks (PY6f's allowThreads; queue 200, PY6-core)"] [1668 45 "// fexecve"] [1721 3 "// abort(3): death by SIGABRT, its action SIG_DFL first (py-os-1124: Go's runtime handles SIGABRT, so the kill"] [1722 3 "// alone ended the process otherwise; test_subprocess's test_run_abort), stdout's buffer lost as C's abort loses it"] [1728 2 "// ---- configuration"] [1817 1 "// sysconfDynamic is musl's sysconf of the values it computes (src/conf/sysconf.c)."] [1836 10 "// SC_ARG_MAX"] [1841 10 "// SC_CHILD_MAX"] [1843 10 "// SC_OPEN_MAX"] [1845 11 "// SC_PAGESIZE (SC_PAGE_SIZE)"] [1847 15 "// SC_NPROCESSORS_CONF, SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN"] [1849 11 "// SC_PHYS_PAGES"] [1852 11 "// SC_AVPHYS_PAGES"] [1855 12 "// SC_MINSIGSTKSZ: the auxiliary vector's AT_MINSIGSTKSZ, at least MINSIGSTKSZ"] [1883 1 "// ---- DirEntry and scandir's iterator"] [1888 25 "// d_type's bits"] [1889 25 "// d_ino"] [1893 1 "// dirent is one linux_dirent64 of getdents64."] [1900 1 "// readDirents is readdir(3) over getdents64: each entry's name, d_ino and d_type, \".\" and \"..\" left out."] [1932 1 "// mode is d_type as os.FileMode's type bits; DT_UNKNOWN an lstat of the entry, as Go's ReadDir does."] [1966 1 "// scandirFinalize is ScandirIterator_finalize (queue 241): an iterator not closed (nor exhausted) warns"] [1967 1 "// ResourceWarning \"unclosed scandir iterator %R\" (its source the iterator) and is closed."] [2112 1 "// openDir is opendir(3): the path opened O_DIRECTORY, so a FIFO or a file fails at once (os.Open of a FIFO blocks"] [2113 1 "// until a writer opens it: os.walk of a named pipe hung)."] [2122 1 "// posixMinArgs are the positional arguments posix's functions need (Argument Clinic's required ones), so that a"] [2123 1 "// short call is a TypeError, never an index past args (a Go panic ended test_os's driver in test_readinto_badarg)."] [2135 1 "// posixMaxArgs are the arguments of posix's functions that take a fixed few: none for the no-argument functions"] [2136 1 "// (testNoArgFunctions), more a TypeError."] [2162 1 "// devConv is a dev_t argument (_Py_Dev_Converter): an int of 64 bits, -1 NODEV; max the bound of major's and"] [2163 1 "// minor's unsigned int when not 0."] [2185 1 "// The system interface where TamaGo's syscall lacks it (queue 214: pyi's runtime listed in goi's table, checked in its"] [2186 1 "// tamago configurations too; builtins_os_other.go there): Linux's."] [2192 1 "// oNofollow is O_NOFOLLOW, the architecture's (a function: the constant's value differs between amd64 and arm64)."] [2197 1 "// ignorePipeSignals ignores SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ, as CPython's startup does."] [2208 1 "// sigOSIgnored is whether the process's action for signal n is SIG_IGN (rt_sigaction's query; py-mods-1122)."] [2210 27 "// struct sigaction: the handler first (amd64's and arm64's alike)"] [2217 1 "// sigOSDefault sets the process's action for signal n to SIG_DFL (py-mods-1122): Go's signal.Reset keeps a SIGHUP or"] [2218 1 "// SIGINT ignored at the process's start ignored (the runtime respects that inherited SIG_IGN), where CPython's"] [2219 1 "// signal.signal(n, SIG_DFL) sets the default, which a child then inherits (test_asyncio's test_send_signal: a child"] [2220 1 "// started after signal.signal(SIGHUP, SIG_DFL) by a driver started with SIGHUP ignored ignored the SIGHUP it was sent)."] [2222 27 "// SIG_DFL, no flags, an empty mask"]] :go/pos {:name [3 9] :package [3 1]} :go/semis [[48 13] [48 21] [81 22] [91 45] [95 23] [107 24] [139 22] [146 48] [147 24] [164 27] [165 83] [185 24] [192 48] [234 22] [249 37] [287 34] [369 35] [370 85] [374 30] [395 32] [410 25] [430 31] [456 35] [467 20] [509 25] [523 30] [531 24] [559 20] [581 29] [588 35] [633 31] [666 21] [670 40] [704 37] [708 41] [711 41] [714 31] [718 30] [735 21] [774 24] [777 25] [794 36] [797 36] [893 29] [894 30] [931 37] [951 76] [971 36] [978 53] [1079 30] [1084 49] [1093 38] [1111 15] [1111 24] [1118 51] [1129 36] [1181 35] [1209 35] [1212 32] [1223 44] [1239 59] [1246 43] [1267 35] [1410 28] [1469 30] [1500 13] [1500 34] [1507 27] [1512 86] [1553 60] [1685 35] [1733 23] [1741 23] [1754 32] [1757 31] [1767 32] [1794 35] [1810 31] [1837 41] [1860 46] [1861 14] [1861 30] [1864 38] [1877 12] [1877 20] [1915 15] [1915 28] [1921 46] [1924 25] [1950 30] [1974 68] [2106 87] [2149 32] [2165 22] [2202 55] [2211 97]]} (go/file "builtins_posix_ext.go" :build ["//go:build linux"]